From 7f02f61c11f91c7bd33ebcd74fa98488217ba366 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Haiku 5.5" <a@b>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:23:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rv1126b: rkcommon row for the RV1126B V2 idblock, and an
 exact name match (6 of 6)

Adds the rkcommon row for the RV1126B idblock (tools/rkcommon.c), and fixes the row lookup it exposed.

Row: { "rv1126b", "110F", 0x10000 - 0x1000, false, RK_HEADER_V2 }. Facts, all from disk:
- RKBOOT/RV1126BMINIALL.ini (rkbin 3e288fe): NAME=RV110F at line 2 (the boot ROM's chip tag, 110F);
  NEWIDB=true at line 25 (the V2 idblock); 471_RC4_OFF and RC4_OFF at lines 27-28 (spl_rc4 false);
  LOAD_ADDR=0x4fe00000 at line 20 (the SPL load address, the seed's CONFIG_SPL_TEXT_BASE).
- The size limit 0x10000 - 0x1000 is the 64 KiB system SRAM at 0x3ffb0000 less the 4 KiB header
  block, the rk3568 and rk3576 rows' convention. The SPL is 78027 bytes, far under it.
- For V2 rows spl_hdr is a label, not written into the image: the image starts with the RK_MAGIC_V2
  word ("RKNS"), and the rv1126b row prints as "Rockchip 110F boot image".
UNVERIFIED until a board boots an image built with it.

Fix (shared code, minimal): the lookup in rkcommon_get_spl_info compared only the first six characters
(strncmp(..., 6)), so "rv1126b" matched the rv1126 row (its first six characters) and was packed with
the 110B header. It now compares the whole name. Every existing name is unchanged: each one is an exact
image name.

Checked: tools-only builds rkcommon.o with 0 warnings. mkimage -n rv1126b -T rksd -d <rkbin DDR blob>:<SPL>
produces a "RKNS" header with the 110F label; -n rv1126 still produces 110B.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/rkcommon.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/rkcommon.c b/tools/rkcommon.c
index b39777fc..4cab3f71 100644
--- a/tools/rkcommon.c
+++ b/tools/rkcommon.c
@@ -155,6 +155,12 @@ static struct spl_info spl_infos[] = {
 	{ "rk3588", "RK35", 0x100000 - 0x1000, false, RK_HEADER_V2 },
 	{ "rv1108", "RK11", 0x1800, false, RK_HEADER_V1 },
 	{ "rv1126", "110B", 0x10000 - 0x1000, false, RK_HEADER_V1 },
+	/* RV1126B (Luckfox Aura). UNVERIFIED until a board boots it. The boot ROM chip tag is 110F
+	 * (RKBOOT/RV1126BMINIALL.ini line 2, NAME=RV110F). NEWIDB=true (line 25) makes this a V2 idblock: the
+	 * image starts with RK_MAGIC_V2 ("RKNS"), and spl_hdr is only a label on V2 rows (rk3568 and rk3576 use
+	 * "RK35" for the family). Size limit: the 64 KiB system SRAM at 0x3ffb0000 (BSP dtsi system_sram), with
+	 * the rk3568 and rk3576 rows' 0x1000 reserve. RC4 is off (RC4_OFF=true, line 28; 471_RC4_OFF line 27). */
+	{ "rv1126b", "110F", 0x10000 - 0x1000, false, RK_HEADER_V2 },
 };
 
 /**
@@ -188,7 +194,8 @@ static struct spl_info *rkcommon_get_spl_info(char *imagename)
 		return NULL;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(spl_infos); i++)
-		if (!strncmp(imagename, spl_infos[i].imagename, 6))
+		/* exact match: strncmp(..., 6) made "rv1126b" match the "rv1126" row (its first 6 characters) */
+		if (!strcmp(imagename, spl_infos[i].imagename))
 			return spl_infos + i;
 
 	return NULL;
